" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570690 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186570542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570690 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f1720c0f-a588-5d99-8985-6683833889bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570765 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570765 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570765 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570765 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/cc/cc2ea14272a30271bb022e9deb5e8b506ed0c2725d6633e7308b3786cb09d84c.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570765 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9e5a7d0-a42d-53f5-8ae1-26c9c5fee794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570765 #edb/ref 1074 "We see from the graph that as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the left, the function $f(x)$ approaches $-\\infty .$ So, the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nLikewise, as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the right, the function $f(x)$ again approaches $-\\infty .$ So, the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570767 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570767 #edb/ref 1069 "q-338954" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570767 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570767 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8c/8c0a344d98dc0ca3a6e4c0fdc3c98074bc2de23301300e663a02ea6f4dff3035.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Therefore\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,6}f(x)=$\n\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570767 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae5c5c63-a42c-5945-a9b3-a559880f74b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570767 #edb/ref 1074 "We see from the graph that as $x$ approaches $6$ from the left, the function $f(x)$ approaches $\\infty .$ So, the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {6}^{-}}f(x)=\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nLikewise, as $x$ approaches $6$ from the right, the function $f(x)$ again approaches $\\infty .$ So, the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {6}^{+}}f(x)=\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 6}f(x)=\\infty \\,.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570768 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570768 #edb/ref 1069 "q-51034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570768 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570768 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/84/84490ed5dee30eb93ae322d0d4ca20109672a80083bf9eabb252ae49c7501036.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570768 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2b0f174-efe7-5216-b895-6e427b351bde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570768 #edb/ref 1074 "As $x$ approaches $5$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty$, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is not defined for $x>5,$ and consequently, we cannot approach $x=5$ from the right. So we have \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n  \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570771 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570771 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570771 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570771 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d1/d1e5821252dd0634c6033a35247af033bcda8a96fa3733b65be52565a60ea3a6.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\,-2}f(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570771 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8283679-623f-5e9d-b3dc-5a2b30321fdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570771 #edb/ref 1074 "As $x$ approaches $-2$ from the right, the function value $f(x)$ grows to infinity, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)=\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, as $x$ approaches $-2$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty$, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570803 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570803 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c87e3a0-0132-57e9-9e94-d890526a21d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570803 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570811 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570811 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3ede1871-f5b8-5de6-b960-f025a0d82481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570811 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570819 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570819 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "51ae2c5a-962e-5d21-8c31-b89b3b4db781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570819 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570866 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "df01aa43-5f29-55b3-96cc-9f5e0a72a50a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570866 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570767 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
